    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 3.92,
      "text": "How does an approved decision become organized delivery work?"
    },
    {
      "start": 4.14,
      "end": 9.34,
      "text": "EMOS uses deterministic wave planning and disposition-specific workflows to structure"
    },
    {
      "start": 9.34,
      "end": 10.34,
      "text": "the next steps."
    },
    {
      "start": 10.34,
      "end": 15.94,
      "text": "Review wave sequencing, readiness actions, stage owners, blockers, and checkpoint"
    },
    {
      "start": 15.94,
      "end": 16.76,
      "text": "requirements."
    },
    {
      "start": 17.28,
      "end": 20.7,
      "text": "The chosen six R disposition determines the downstream playbook."
    },
    {
      "start": 20.7,
      "end": 26.24,
      "text": "Needs Evidence and unapproved workloads cannot enter or advance governed execution."
    },
    {
      "start": 26.919999999999998,
      "end": 31.46,
      "text": "Resolve evidence gaps and record explicit human approval before progressing through"
    },
    {
      "start": 31.46,
      "end": 31.979999999999997,
      "text": "the workflow."
    },
    {
      "start": 31.979999999999997,
      "end": 34.459999999999994,
      "text": "These are planning and tracking controls."
    },
    {
      "start": 35.0,
      "end": 40.239999999999995,
      "text": "EMOS does not run a real cloud migration, provision infrastructure, or perform a"
    },
    {
      "start": 40.239999999999995,
      "end": 41.379999999999995,
      "text": "production cutover."
    },
    {
      "start": 41.839999999999996,
      "end": 46.66,
      "text": "Next, review the current blocker and assign the required evidence or delivery action"
    },
    {
      "start": 46.66,
      "end": 48.019999999999996,
      "text": "to its accountable owner."
    }
  ],
